    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\n[mini.files]\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI find having columns that constantly change in size distracting. I have modified it in the config to show only 1 column. I would like mini.files to open as a buffer instead of a floating window so that when I have several splits, mini.files opens in the split where the command is invoked. Can this be done?",
