        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am afraid, no: 'mini.files' explorer will always be possible to open *only* as temporary floating windows.\r\n\r\nIf changing widths is the main problem here, then it can be adjusted by setting the same [`config.windows.width_*`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0a8a1072137d916406507c941698a4bfa9dbbe7a/doc/mini-files.txt#L602-L607) values. This will make all windows have same width while still allowing to show the current branch via Miller columns. The currently focused window can then by identified via title which will be highlighted with [`MiniFilesTitleFocused`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0a8a1072137d916406507c941698a4bfa9dbbe7a/doc/mini-files.txt#L97) highlight group.",
