        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> It is both width and height. At the moment, it completely covers over lualine, which doesn't look nice.\r\n\r\nThen you can adjust it with `config.height = vim.api.nvim_win_get_height(0) - 1`. Note that it will limit height to the height of current window which might be smaller if there are vertically stacked splits. You can use `config.height = vim.o.lines - vim.o.cmdheight - 1` to make it span whole instance height.\r\n\r\nAlso note that `-- Ensure title padding` paragraph is not needed for adjusting height.",
