            "body": "Thanks for the replies. These are not proper solutions. I had tried something like that but it looks bad when size of neovim window changes. Also, the way you have things setup at the moment does not allow the width to be changed dynamically. So, it almost impossible to have it look nice. I have tried `oil`. While it works as I would like it to work, it has a weird flickering when I go up a directory. Looks like I have to go back to using `nnn`.",
