        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> I am afraid, no: 'mini.files' explorer will always be possible to open _only_ as temporary floating windows.\r\n> \r\n> If changing widths is the main problem here, then it can be adjusted by setting the same [`config.windows.width_*`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0a8a1072137d916406507c941698a4bfa9dbbe7a/doc/mini-files.txt#L602-L607) values. This will make all windows have same width while still allowing to show the current branch via Miller columns. The currently focused window can then by identified via title which will be highlighted with [`MiniFilesTitleFocused`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0a8a1072137d916406507c941698a4bfa9dbbe7a/doc/mini-files.txt#L97) highlight group.\r\n\r\nThank you SO MUCH! This is what I've looking for a long time (without knowing they were called \"MIller Columns\" xD). I believe there are many other plugins that try to do this, without knowing this is already possible here. Might I suggest to put this in a more visible place, maybe a wiki? ",
            "created_at": "2024-11-05T13:09:33Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1322#issuecomment-2457125675",
            "id": 2457125675,
