        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Thank you SO MUCH! This is what I've looking for a long time (without knowing they were called \"MIller Columns\" xD). I believe there are many other plugins that try to do this, without knowing this is already possible here. Might I suggest to put this in a more visible place, maybe a wiki?\r\n\r\nI mean... Config structure is documented both in [help file](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c8bc67a35e627908da644c5f8cd26b3f987f2627/doc/mini-files.txt#L596-L608) and [module's README](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-files.md#default-config). If the goal is to have windows have same width, then looking for something that configures windows seems like a common sense.\r\n\r\nOne thing that might be worth adding to the (planned in some type of future) wiki is the code snippet for a \"static\" layout which respects Neovim instance window resize. Same as described in this issue, with `VimResized` callback, etc.",
